cked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2020-12-15T12:59:37Z","updated_at":"2020-12-15T13:58:52Z","closed_at":"2020-12-15T13:58:52Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nv1.4 Documentation at ORM extensions | Hybrid Attributes states:\r\n\r\n> When dealing with the Interval class itself, the hybrid_property descriptor evaluates the function body given the Interval class as the argument, which when evaluated with SQLAlchemy expression mechanics returns a new SQL expression:\r\n\r\n```\r\n>>> print(Interval.length)\r\ninterval.\"end\" - interval.start\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstead of getting the expected `interval.\"end\" - interval.start` I get `Interval.length`.\r\nI am running SQLAlchemy 1.4.0b, Python 3.9  on macOS BigSur 11.0.1\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nThe expected result is as described in the manual.\r\n\r\n**The fix?**\r\nThe expected result can be produced if the following code is substituted:\r\n```\r\n print(f\"{Interval.length.expression}\")\r\n```\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"